Now I understand the vulnerability. Let me analyze `GetSsmlAttribute`:

```c
static wchar_t *GetSsmlAttribute(wchar_t *pw, const char *name)
{
        int ix;
        static wchar_t empty[1] = { 0 };

        while (*pw != 0) {
                if (iswspace(pw[-1])) {
                        ...
                }
                pw++;
        }
        return NULL;
}
```

The issue is `pw[-1]`. When `pw` points to the first character of the string (index 0), `pw[-1]` reads one wchar_t before the start of the buffer. This is an out-of-bounds read.

